  // Pages are filled with as many *complete* paragraphs as fit. A paragraph
  // is never split across a page boundary — it either fits on the current
  // page in full, or it starts the next page instead. That means a page can
  // occasionally end a little short of the bottom margin, but every
  // paragraph always reads as one continuous block, with its indent and
